  + Days 249–264. **Several things yoyo used to do quietly it now refuses or asks about, and one key stopped travelling.** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is sent only to `--provider anthropic`; `/save`, `/export` and `/spawn -o` refuse to replace an existing file without `--force`; a bash command the new parse tree can't read asks for confirmation even under "always" or an allow rule; a `.yoyo.toml` that isn't valid TOML stops the run with the file and line; and `--provider custom` (or an unknown provider wi… [yoyo: 493 more bytes elided — diff lines are capped at 500 bytes]
  + 
  + ### Changed (behaviour you will notice)
  + 
  + - **`/save`, `/export` and `/spawn -o` refuse to overwrite an existing file.** Each says `<path> already exists. Nothing was written.` and names the `--force` form; `/spawn -o` refuses before the sub-agent runs, so nothing is spent. `/save` still replaces a file it wrote itself this session. `--save-session <path>` and the CLI `--output`/`-o` flag still replace silently (#1211; the remainder is #1214).
  + - **Bash commands are checked on a parse tree, and what the tree can't read asks.** yoyo now parses each command with tree-sitter-bash and runs its safety checks on every simple command in it, including the bodies of a literal `bash -c "…"` / `sh -c '…'` (#1209). A parse error, `eval`, or a command name chosen by an expansion goes to confirmation, even after "always" or under an exact allow rule. A wildcard allow rule (`git *`, `cargo *`, `*`) auto-approves only a single plain command, so `g… [yoyo: 248 more bytes elided — diff lines are capped at 500 bytes]
  + - **A `.yoyo.toml` that isn't valid TOML stops the run.** Every loaded config file is parsed with the `toml` crate at startup; a syntax error prints the file, line and column, and nothing is sent (#1184, still open for the remaining line readers).
  + - **`--provider custom` (or an unknown OpenAI-compatible provider) with no model named refuses** instead of sending `claude-opus-5-5` to your own server; the REPL's `/provider` does the same (#1175, #1183).
  + - **`--provider github` is refused**: GitHub Models was retired on 2026-07-30, and its endpoint answers every path with a plain-text `OK`. The setup wizard and README no longer offer it (#1166).
  + - **`-p` exits non-zero when the reply was cut by a limit you didn't set, or refused**, and `--output-format json` gains an `incomplete` key (`null`, `{reason: output_limit, limit_set_by}`, or `{reason: refusal}`) with `is_error` agreeing with the exit code; stream-json prints the same note on stderr (#1026).
  + - **`yoyo -p hi extra` refuses the stray word** (exit 2, nothing sent) instead of silently dropping it, and the refusal names a flag that swallowed another flag as its value (#1150, #1151).
  + - **`--temperature` is not sent to Claude 4.7 and later** (Anthropic removed it for those models); yoyo says so on stderr. Elsewhere the accepted range follows the vendor: up to 2.0 where the provider documents 0–2, 1.0 otherwise, and `/config set temperature` accepts only what the run would send (#1145, #1204, #1207).
  + - **GIF is no longer accepted by `/add`, `@path` or `--image`** (yoagent 0.27 refuses it), and every "supported formats" message comes from one list (#1143).
    
