I cut v0.5.0 and pushed the tag. The release workflow has started but not finished: run 44534327944 was still queued after about 9 minutes, waiting for a runner. Nothing has reached crates.io yet. I didn't retry anything and didn't run cargo publish myself.

What I did
• Version: bumped 0.4.0 → 0.5.0 in Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock. yoyo --version now prints yoyo v0.5.0. The only other "0.4.0" in the tree is a docs sentence about the past ("Up to yoyo 0.4.0…"), which is still correct, so I left it.
• CHANGELOG: there's an empty [Unreleased] heading on top, then ## [0.5.0] - 2026-11-19. It opens with a summary of the behaviour changes users will notice:
  • ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is only sent to Anthropic.
  • /save, /export and /spawn -o refuse to overwrite a file without --force.
  • Bash commands the parser can't read now ask for confirmation.
  • A .yoyo.toml that isn't valid TOML stops the run.
  • --provider custom with no model, and --provider github, are refused.

  After that come Security, Fixed, Added, Dependencies (yoagent 0.26.8 → 0.27.9, plus tree-sitter, toml and rustls-native-certs) and a price audit note. I checked every issue number with gh issue view, and the open ones are labelled as still open (#1012, #1094, #1147, #1184, #1202, #1206, #1210, #1214, #1216).
• Commit and tag: commit 55b4b0c0. git ls-remote shows refs/tags/v0.5.0 on origin.

Gates (run on the 0.5.0 tree): build, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all passed, and cargo test exited 0 with nothing failing. I edited the CHANGELOG after that run, so I re-ran the two test files that read it; both passed. cargo publish --dry-run --no-verify packages fine, with warnings that two dependencies in the lockfile (chacha20 0.10.0, clipboard-win 5.4.1) have been yanked.

Prices: shipped with known drift
• DeepSeek audit: passed, but it compared 0 rows. All four DeepSeek ids it can see are registered exceptions, and models.dev doesn't list deepseek-r1 or deepseek-v3, so nothing checks those.
• General audit: SUMMARY compared 115, matched 54, drifted 48, cache_read_only 13, unpriced 69 of 184 catalogue rows (rel_tol 1%). That's 48 rows where our prices disagree with models.dev, up from 23 at v0.4.0. 12 of them differ only in the cache-write rate.
• I didn't fix any of them, because I didn't read the vendors' pricing pages this session. I posted all 48 rows on the open price-audit issue #1012, and the CHANGELOG names #1012 as their owner. /cost figures for those models may be wrong in either direction. I didn't change any assertion or tolerance.

Two other things
• The repo checkout was shallow, so the first v0.4.0..HEAD log stopped partway; that's where the plan's "50 commits" came from. After fetching more history the real span is 483 commits, about 90 of them task commits.
• I found no open issues or journal entries where someone was promised a heads-up when the next release came out, so I didn't ping anyone.

To see if the publish went through: gh run list --workflow release.yml -L 1. If it fails, look into it tomorrow rather than retrying today.
